    "## Q4. Cognitive-Assistive System — Ordinary Least Squares"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b341476e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = np.array([\n",
    "    [6, 70, 3],\n",
    "    [5, 50, 6],\n",
    "    [8, 80, 2],\n",
    "    [4, 30, 8]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "y = np.array([40, 65, 30, 85])\n",
    "\n",
    "# a. Shape and dimensions\n",
    "print(\"Shape of X:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Dimensions of X:\", X.ndim)\n",
    "\n",
    "# b. Transpose\n",
    "XT = X.T\n",
    "print(\"\\nX.T:\")\n",
    "print(XT)\n",
    "\n",
    "# c. Matrix product X.T @ X\n",
    "XTX = XT @ X\n",
    "print(\"\\nX.T @ X:\")\n",
    "print(XTX)\n",
    "\n",
    "# d. Matrix inverse\n",
    "XTX_inv = np.linalg.inv(XTX)\n",
    "print(\"\\nInverse of X.T @ X:\")\n",
    "print(XTX_inv)\n",
    "\n",
    "# e. Ordinary Least Squares: beta = (X.T X)^(-1) X.T y\n",
    "beta = XTX_inv @ XT @ y\n",
    "print(\"\\nOLS coefficients (beta):\")\n",
    "print(beta)\n",
    "\n",
    "# f. Interpret coefficients\n",
    "print(\"\\nCoefficient interpretation:\")\n",
    "print(\"Sleep coefficient:\", beta[0])\n",
    "print(\"Activity coefficient:\", beta[1])\n",
    "print(\"Stress coefficient:\", beta[2])\n",
    "\n",
    "# g. Predict assistance score for new user\n",
    "new_user = np.array([5, 40, 7])\n",
    "predicted_score = new_user @ beta\n",
    "print(\"\\nPredicted assistance score:\", predicted_score)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e3cf796",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Q4 Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "The transpose `X.T` changes the matrix so that the three feature columns become rows. Thus, it represents the same data organized feature-wise rather than user-wise.\n",
    "\n",
    "The OLS coefficients indicate the estimated change in the assistance score associated with a one-unit change in each feature, **while the other features are held constant**, according to this fitted linear model.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `beta[0]` → estimated coefficient for Sleep Hours.\n",
    "- `beta[1]` → estimated coefficient for Activity Level.\n",
    "- `beta[2]` → estimated coefficient for Stress Level.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a new user `[5, 40, 7]`, the predicted assistance score is calculated as the dot product of the new user's feature vector and the OLS coefficient vector."
   ]
  }
